# @PROJECT@ - Claude queue

The watcher runs the FIRST `## ` section whose heading says status `open`. Only a COMMITTED change to that
section starts a run. Stage later work below it with status `staged`; flip it to `open` when its turn comes.

Format of a section:

    ## <feature id>: <title> - status: `open`
    **Why:** one line, in the owner's words where possible.
    - **<piece id>** <title> [tier: feature] brief: `docs/briefs/<piece id>.md` branch: `task/<piece id>-<slug>` slices: `<piece id>.1,<piece id>.2`

Rules:
- One piece = one draft PR on one `task/...` branch. Each slice brief lives at `docs/briefs/<slice id>.md`.
- Tag every piece: `[tier: security|fix|debug|feature]` or `[model: <id>]`. Security-tier pieces keep their own short PR.
- Close a piece by adding `<piece id> closed` to the heading or `status: \`closed\`` to its bullet.
- If a piece is too big, Claude stops with `LOOP: blocked too big`; the CTO re-splits it (`<id>.1`, `<id>.2`).
- Leave a slice out of `slices:` to keep the watcher from retrying it.

